    feat(ctx): add observability package and /stats + /stats-history endpoints
    
    Implement the Context Orchestrator observability surface (plan 17,
    TICKET-09): a per-request bucket writer that folds proxy savings into
    ctx_stats_history, a periodic rollup runner, and the Stats / StatsHistory
    readers that back the new read-only HTTP endpoints.
    
    - Add mnemonic/internal/ctx/observability package: Roll (pure per-saving
      bucket computation), WriteSavings (per-request fold), Recompute (periodic
      re-derivation), StartRollup (background goroutine), Snapshot (live
      session metrics), StatsHistory (durable savings history). All readers and
      writers are fail-open (ADR-0016): missing ctx_* tables degrade to
      empty/zero, never a hard error.
    - Add GET /stats handler: returns live session-metric snapshot from
      ctx_proxy_sessions (tokens saved, cache hits, requests, sessions, latest
      mode). Zero-valued when no sessions exist.
    - Add GET /stats-history handler: returns durable savings history from
      ctx_stats_history for the granularities configured in
      cfg.Observability.HistoryRollups (defaults to hourly/daily/weekly/monthly).
      Every requested granularity appears in the response, possibly empty.
    - Wire both routes into the mnemonic serve mux via registerCtxRoutes(); they
      live on the serve mux, not the proxy loopback mux, so no collision with
      the proxy own /stats + /v1/compress routes.
    - Add 7 observability unit tests (Roll, WriteSavings merge, Recompute
      session correction, StartRollup goroutine, Snapshot, StatsHistory
      persistence, fail-open) and 4 HTTP handler tests (fail-open default,
      seeded sessions, fail-open history, seeded buckets).
    
